{"text": "Conservative\n\ngroups push\ndevelopment\n\nBy DICK MANNING\nof the Missoulian\n\nThe lastest political umbrella\ncovering pro-development forces\nin the West is woven from threads\nof earlier land-use battles: the\nSagebrush Rebellion and James\nWatt\u2019s Mountain States Legal\nFoundation, for instance.\nThere is a new wrinkle, how-\never, in the coalition of as many\nas 200 groups cailing itself the\n\u201ctwise-use\u2019\u2019 movement. The coali-\ntion, which includes the Commu-\nnities for a Great Northwest in\nwestern Montana and Rep. Ron\nMarlenee\u2019s Montana PLUS. has\nstrong ties to a group that was in\npart bankrolled by Rev. Sun\nMyung Moon\u2019s Unification\nChurch.\nLeaders within the movement\nsay there is no influence by the\ncontroversial Korean religious\ncult.\n\u201cThe Unification Church is\nnot a part of the  wise-use\nmovement. Period. The end,\"\nRon Arnold, a key player in the\nmovement, said in a telephone in-\nterview. \u201cThis happens to be the\neasiest stick with which you can\nbear it (the wise-use movement).\u201d\u201d\nHowever, Arnold and others\n\n*See COALITION. Pave 4.7)\n\nmagazine. \u2018It\u2019s called the\nwise-use movement.\u201d\n\u201cThe members of the\nwise-use Movement ...\nhave the strongest: betief\nthat thelr ieee ed i nha",
